 ],
 "notes": "Defaults enable no subnet tiers, so the plan holds only the VPC; every optional tier is checked via __declared__. Variable names are not pinned (prompt does not name them); the three tier toggles are counted as boolean variables. Subnet CIDR calculation: every declared subnet must use cidrsubnet() or a local whose name states it holds CIDRs; the log-based newbits value lives in a local in the GT and is not observable. Candidate review: GLM53F and Gemini38F set map_public_ip_on_launch=false and scope egress to the VPC CIDR, contradicting the prompt, so public_subnet_autoip and sg_egress_all stay strict. The 'local VPC CIDR route' is not checked: every route table has the local route implicitly, so omitting it already satisfies the prompt and any check would be vacuous. Known Partial: rt_assoc_subnets is not bound to the public subnets specifically."
}
